; Tests for -indvars-allow-reorder-traps: when the exact backedge-taken count
; is unknown *only* because of an unanalyzable trap exit, predicateLoopExits
; may still predicate the leading run of dominating trap exits using a
; symbolic upper bound.  Only trap exits may be forced to fire early, so the
; program still traps -- an abort can never become a normal return.

declare void @llvm.trap()

