; unanalyzable trap exit (mid -> trap2, count is CouldNotCompute due to the
; mul-nuw overflow check) and the latch.  With the flag on, trap1's condition
; is hoisted to a loop-invariant compare against the symbolic-max BTC; the
; unanalyzable trap and the latch are left alone.  With the flag off, nothing
; changes (exact BTC is CouldNotCompute, so the pass bails).
